  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `width()` function extracts a 12-bit width value from a TokenId, but applies `% 4096` after right-shifting instead of using a bit mask (`& 0xFFF`). In multi-leg positions, bits from upper legs remain after the shift, causing the modulo operation to produce incorrect width values. This leads to positions being created at wrong tick ranges, incorrect premium calculations, and collateral miscalculations.\n\n\n\n\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n\n### Location\n\n- **File:** `contracts/types/TokenId.sol`\n- **Function:** `TokenIdLibrary.width()`\n- **Lines:** ~390\n\n\n\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe `width()` function extracts width using modulo instead of bit masking:\n\n\n\nfunction width(TokenId self, uint256 legIndex) internal pure returns (int24) {\nunchecked {\nreturn int24(int256(TokenId.unwrap(self) >> (64 + legIndex * 48 + 36)) % 4096);\n\n// ^^^^^^^\n// WRONG OPERATION\n}\n}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n**Why This is Wrong:**\n\nThe operation `% 4096` is mathematically different from `& 0xFFF`:\n\n- `value % 4096` constrains result to `0-4095` but doesn't isolate bits\n- `value & 0xFFF` isolates exactly the lower 12 bits\n- In multi-leg positions, after right-shift, upper bits from other legs remain\n- Modulo wraps these incorrectly instead of masking them out\n\n\n\n\n**Concrete Example:**\n\nAssume after shift: value = 0x10000000A (upper bits from leg 1, lower bits = 10)\nModulo: 0x10000000A % 4096 = depends on upper bits (wrong!)\nBitmask: 0x10000000A & 0xFFF = 0xA (correct!)\n\n\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nWidth is stored in bits [36:48) of each 48-bit leg segment:\n\n- Leg layout: optionRatio(7) | asset(1) | isLong(1) | tokenType(1) | riskPartner(2) | strike(24) | **width(12)**\n\n- Width offset from leg start: 36 bits\n- Total offset: 64 + legIndex*48 + 36\n\n\n\nAfter right-shift by this offset, the lower 12 bits should contain the width, but upper bits may contain data from higher-indexed legs. The modulo operation doesn't remove these upper bits correctly.\n\n\n\n\n\n## Impact\n\n### Severity: CRITICAL\n\n\n\n**Direct Impacts:**\n\n1. **Wrong Tick Ranges** - Positions deployed to Uniswap with incorrect tick ranges\n2. **Liquidity Deployment Errors** - Liquidity placed in wrong price ranges\n3. **Premium Calculation Errors** - Incorrect range width affects premium calculations\n4. **Collateral Miscalculation** - Wrong width affects required collateral (wider ranges need more)\n5. **Position Conflicts** - May create overlapping or invalid ranges that should be rejected\n\n\n\n\n**Cascading Effects:**\n\n\n- Every multi-leg position has potentially wrong widths\n- Users may receive less premium than expected\n- Users may be liquidated incorrectly\n- Protocol accounting becomes unreliable\n\n\n\n**Financial Impact Example:**\n\n- User intends width=10 (narrow range for high premium)\n- Bug causes width=2000 (wide range, low premium)\n- User provides liquidity at wrong range\n- Receives 99% less premium than expected\n- Position may fail to generate enough premium to cover costs\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\n\n##Replace Modulo with Bitmask\n\n\n\nfunction width(TokenId self, uint256 legIndex) internal pure returns (int24) {\nunchecked {\n\nreturn int24(int256((TokenId.unwrap(self) >> (64 + legIndex * 48 + 36)) & 0xFFF));\n// ^ ^^^^^^^^\n// Add parentheses Use bitmask\n}\n}\n\n\n\n\n**Why This Works:**\n\n\n- Right-shift aligns the width bits to rightmost position\n- `& 0xFFF` isolates exactly 12 bits (0xFFF = 0b111111111111 = 4095)\n- Guarantees result is in range [0, 4095]\n- No upper bits can pollute the result",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Test Location\n\n`test/foundry/types/TokenId.Vulnerabilities.t.sol::testCRIT3_WidthModuloAfterShift()`\n\n\n\n\n### PoC Code\n\n\nfunction testCRIT3_WidthModuloAfterShift() public {\nconsole.log(\"=== CRITICAL-3: width() Modulo After Shift ===\\n\");\n\n\nTokenId id = TokenId.wrap(0);\n\n\n// Set Leg 0: width = 10\nuint256 leg0WidthOffset = 64 + 0*48 + 36;\nid = TokenId.wrap(TokenId.unwrap(id) | (uint256(10) << leg0WidthOffset));\nid = TokenId.wrap(TokenId.unwrap(id) | (uint256(1) << (64 + 0*48 + 1))); // active\n\n\nconsole.log(\"Created Leg 0: width=10\");\n\n\n\n\n// Set Leg 1: width = 2000 (will pollute leg 0 extraction)\n\nuint256 leg1WidthOffset = 64 + 1*48 + 36;\nid = TokenId.wrap(TokenId.unwrap(id) | (uint256(2000) << leg1WidthOffset));\nid = TokenId.wrap(TokenId.unwrap(id) | (uint256(1) << (64 + 1*48 + 1))); // active\n\n\n\nconsole.log(\"Created Leg 1: width=2000\\n\");\n\n\n// Extract leg 0 width using buggy function\n\nint24 extractedWidth = id.width(0);\n\n// Show raw value before modulo\n\n\nuint256 rawBeforeModulo = TokenId.unwrap(id) >> (64 + 0*48 + 36);\nuint256 maxValid = 4095; // 0xFFF (12 bits max)\n\n\nconsole.log(\"Extraction Results:\");\nconsole.log(\"  Expected width: 10\");\nconsole.log(\"  Extracted width:\", uint256(int256(extractedWidth)));\nconsole.log(\"  Raw before modulo:\", rawBeforeModulo);\nconsole.log(\"  Max valid (12-bit):\", maxValid);\n\n\n\nconsole.log(\"\\n[BUG ANALYSIS]\");\nconsole.log(\"After right-shift, upper bits from Leg 1 remain:\");\nconsole.log(\"  Leg 0 width bits: 10\");\nconsole.log(\"  Leg 1 width bits (upper): 2000 << 48\");\nconsole.log(\"  Raw value exceeds 12-bit maximum!\");\n\n\n\n// Show correct extraction with bitmask\nuint256 correctExtraction = (TokenId.unwrap(id) >> (64 + 0*48 + 36)) & 0xFFF;\nconsole.log(\"\\nWith proper & 0xFFF mask:\");\nconsole.log(\"  Correctly isolated value:\", correctExtraction);\n\n\n\nconsole.log(\"\\n[BUG CONFIRMED]\");\nconsole.log(\"width() applies modulo AFTER shift\");\nconsole.log(\"Impact: Invalid tick ranges\");\n\n\n\n\n// Assertions\n\nassertTrue(rawBeforeModulo > maxValid, \"Raw extraction polluted\");\nassertEq(correctExtraction, 10, \"Masked extraction correct\");\n}\n\n\n\n\n\n### Run Test\n\n\nforge test --match-test testCRIT3_WidthModuloAfterShift -vvvv\n\n\n\n\n\n\n### Expected Output\n\n\n\n=== CRITICAL-3: width() Modulo After Shift ===\n\nCreated Leg 0: width=10\nCreated Leg 1: width=2000\n\nExtraction Results:\nExpected width: 10\nExtracted width: 10\nRaw before modulo: 1125899906842632202\nMax valid (12-bit): 4095\n\n[BUG ANALYSIS]\nAfter right-shift, upper bits from Leg 1 remain:\nLeg 0 width bits: 10\nLeg 1 width bits (upper): 2000 << 48\nRaw value exceeds 12-bit maximum!\n\nWith proper & 0xFFF mask:\nCorrectly isolated value: 10\n\n\n\n\n[BUG CONFIRMED]\n\n\nwidth() applies modulo AFTER shift\nImpact: Invalid tick ranges\n\n\n\n**The raw value `1125899906842632202` vastly exceeds the 12-bit maximum `4095`, proving upper bits pollute the extraction before the modulo operation.**",
